---
description: How to author a scene in src/scenes
globs: src/scenes/**
alwaysApply: false
---

A scene folder contains exactly index.html and scene.ts.

index.html is markup only: a .stage at true pixel size, a .camera wrapping
.screen beats, a .grain overlay, and chrome (Clips, #replay, #slow, #rec,
#export-mp4, #export-mov, #status). No inline styles. No inline script beyond
<script type="module" src="./scene.ts">.

No eyebrows. No rules. No captions. No labels sitting next to motion.
Text is one centered line. Motion and type never share a screen — conceal
the line, then bring the graph on.

scene.ts calls mountStage once and reads top to bottom as a storyboard using
absolute millisecond timings. Do not nest callbacks. Do not use setTimeout
directly; use tl.at().

Compose from src/lib primitives. If a scene needs a motion behaviour that
does not exist yet, add it to src/lib as a named primitive with a doc comment
explaining why it exists, then use it. Never inline a one-off animation.

A gradient phrase uses data-split="whole". Plain lines that must stay one
unit do the same.

Typical timings for a 10s scene: title 280, conceal 2800, graph screen 3600,
nodes 4000 with step 140, travelling pulse 5200 over 2800.

Imports are relative. No @ or ~ aliases.
